From 46c37fc74450b8703f090691052894710392aa25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: loveyu <i@loveyu.info>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 13:21:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: Accept an existing static picture cache

Static picture handlers create their presentation cache when the handler is
constructed. A subsequent IOleCache::Cache call therefore returns
CACHE_S_SAMECACHE instead of S_OK. Both are successful HRESULTs, but the
static-object insertion path only accepts the latter and aborts before
IRichEditOleCallback::QueryInsertObject.

Accept every successful cache result so enhanced-metafile pictures can reach
the application insertion callback.
---
 dlls/riched20/editor.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/riched20/editor.c b/dlls/riched20/editor.c
index f718b367fe8..b29f361069e 100644
--- a/dlls/riched20/editor.c
+++ b/dlls/riched20/editor.c
@@ -1153,7 +1153,7 @@ static HRESULT insert_static_object(ME_TextEditor *editor, HENHMETAFILE hemf, HB
       IOleObject_SetClientSite(lpObject, lpClientSite) == S_OK &&
       IOleObject_GetUserClassID(lpObject, &clsid) == S_OK &&
       IOleObject_QueryInterface(lpObject, &IID_IOleCache, (void**)&lpOleCache) == S_OK &&
-      IOleCache_Cache(lpOleCache, &fm, 0, &conn) == S_OK &&
+      SUCCEEDED(IOleCache_Cache(lpOleCache, &fm, 0, &conn)) &&
       IOleObject_QueryInterface(lpObject, &IID_IDataObject, (void**)&lpDataObject) == S_OK &&
       IDataObject_SetData(lpDataObject, &fm, &stgm, TRUE) == S_OK)
   {
